file Desktop\TIPS.TXT
	icon: res://win95/theme/icons/document_text_32.png
	modified: Tuesday, May 28, 1996 9:05:33 PM
	contents:
		JOSE'S COMPUTER TIPS
		(for cousin Rafa, who keeps calling me)

		1. Long program names slow Windows down. Shorten them.
		2. ".EXE" is decoration. Windows knows a program when it sees one.
		3. When a box pops up, click it away. That's just Windows talking.
		4. More parts, more heat. Take out what you don't need.
		5. Wear a hat when you work on a computer. Static.

